      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1333681835,
      "text": "Hoya multiflora, commonly known as shooting star hoya, is a species of evergreen tropical plants in the oleander and frangipani family Apocynaceae. It is an epiphytic shrub to about 2.5 m tall, producing large clusters of distinctive \"shooting star\" flowers. It is native to Assam, Bangladesh, southern China, Indo-China and Malesia."
    }
